 "_comment": "Carry-12's cells end to end on CPU at toy size with cell T, 28 Oct 2026 (tests/test_carry12_cells_e2e.py with C12_TOY_SEEDS=1,2,3; WSL, a clean ext4 clone at the commit below, mtstudio CPU build of the same C++ (437db1f2), ember ec3201b CPU). Every machine file's pretraining spec and post command with the VM's paths mapped to the toy's; toy changes: d 64, 2 or 4 layers, a 700-token BPE vocabulary (its text includes every 8th template dialogue, so T's rows fit T 1,024 whole), 4 pretraining and 3 SFT steps, 2,048 tokens per step, 16 panel windows, Carry-5 every 26th item (40), Carry-12 every 110th (14); the chat checks as tools/chat_eval.py on 3 prompts. The toy models are at chance, so every registered contrast reads FLOOR: the gate path is what is exercised.",
